+# INSTALL: the /sc:spec-panel-ledger experiment variant (issue 346, theme ledger)
+
+Owner install by hand for the S1 arm "led". This is not a repo change and runs no `superclaude install`.
+
+## What gets installed
+
+Exactly three files go into `~/.claude/`:
+
+| Repo file | Installed copy |
+|---|---|
+| `src/superclaude/commands/spec-panel-ledger.md` | `~/.claude/commands/sc/spec-panel-ledger.md` |
+| `src/superclaude/skills/sc-review-ledger/SKILL.md` | `~/.claude/skills/sc-review-ledger/SKILL.md` |
+| `src/superclaude/skills/sc-review-ledger/scripts/review_ledger.py` | `~/.claude/skills/sc-review-ledger/scripts/review_ledger.py` |
+
+Run from the repo root (the `bs346-ledger` worktree):
+
+```bash
+cp src/superclaude/commands/spec-panel-ledger.md ~/.claude/commands/sc/
+cp -r src/superclaude/skills/sc-review-ledger ~/.claude/skills/
+sha256sum ~/.claude/commands/sc/spec-panel-ledger.md \
+  ~/.claude/skills/sc-review-ledger/SKILL.md \
+  ~/.claude/skills/sc-review-ledger/scripts/review_ledger.py
+```
+
+Record the three `sha256sum` lines in the install watcher. Nothing else in `~/.claude/` changes: `~/.claude/commands/sc/spec-panel.md` stays as it is, and no `superclaude install` runs. Every worker host needs `uv`: the hosts that run the ledger steps, and also the review and reviser hosts, whose sessions may run `status`, `verdict` and `--dry-run` checks (every call is `uv run --no-project python "<skill base>/scripts/review_ledger.py" ...`, with `<skill base>` = `~/.claude/skills/sc-review-ledger`).
+
+## The variant's base
+
+`spec-panel-ledger.md` is a byte copy of the 472-line Arm B file `/home/coder/workspaces/worktrees/IronClaude/exp346-p1-logs/.dev/experiments/346-validation/phase2/S1/inputs/tool-text/spec-panel-post427-95f2c6e4.md` (sha256 `c8d80346a96cb528fce6cff3bcadfed5bc95d1eee48dea0ac275404314b8df2f`, the PR 427 text the S1 arms ran), with only three blocks changed: the frontmatter `name` and `description`, the Usage line (`/sc:spec-panel-ledger`, no `--re-review`/`--baseline`, adds `[--ledger <dir>] [--revert-unclaimed] [--sweep]`), and `## Review Loop` replaced by `## Review Ledger Loop` (a refusal line for `--unattended` and eight one-line bullets). It is 475 lines.
+
+- The current `src/superclaude/commands/spec-panel.md` was not used as the base: without its `## Unattended mode` section it is 474 lines, two more than the Arm B file (a second Usage line with `--unattended` and a line about `--target-release`). The existing `src/superclaude/commands/spec-panel.md` is not changed.
+- The variant deliberately has no `## Unattended mode` section (owner decision; the base has none), and the S1 briefs never pass `--unattended`. A standalone `--unattended` token is refused with "spec-panel-ledger has no unattended mode".
+- The base inherits one line naming `src/superclaude/examples/release-spec-template.md` (in `## Tool Coordination`). The copy rule wins: the variant keeps that line unchanged, and `tests/skills/test_spec_panel_ledger_command.py` asserts the variant adds no `src/superclaude` occurrence beyond the base's one.
+- The title line `# /sc:spec-panel - Expert Specification Review Panel` and the examples that name `/sc:spec-panel` are byte copies of the base, on purpose.
+- The drift test compares the variant with a byte copy of the base kept as `tests/skills/fixtures/review-ledger/spec-panel-post427-base.md`.
+- `tests/recommend/test_routing_refresh.py` gets `spec-panel-ledger` added to `_POST_REFRESH_ADDITIONS` (owner ruling); nothing else in that file changes.
+- `make lint` reports one warning for the variant (Check 3, 475 lines over the 200-line warn threshold), the same warning `spec-panel.md` already gets; no error.
+
+## The briefs
+
+The one-line substitution (source.md section 4), in the three S1 review briefs only:
+
+```text
+/sc:spec-panel        ->  /sc:spec-panel-ledger --ledger .dev/orca-command-refactor/specs/orca-worker-contract-spec.review-ledger --revert-unclaimed
+```
+
+It applies to T05, T07 and T09; T06, T08 and T10 stay verbatim (T10 is not dispatched: review 3 always ends the loop). All other flags on the line stay. The ready copies are in `.dev/brainstorms/346-ledger/briefs/` with a `README.md` that lists every change and the values filled at dispatch time.
+
+## The ledger steps
+
+Review and reviser sessions never run a script call that writes a file. Every write (`init`, `find`, `answer`, `begin` with its scripted revert, `verify`, `close`, `sweep`) is an inserted coordinator step with its own brief template in `.dev/brainstorms/346-ledger/briefs/ledger-steps/`, run between the S1 tasks in the order its `README.md` gives (`L0-init`, T05, `L-find-close`, T06, `L-begin`, T07, `L-verify-close`, T08, `L-begin`, T09, `L-verify-close`, then the sweep route). Skip rule: after a `close` whose `verdict` exits 12 (the loop ended at review 1 or 2), the remaining T06 to T09 dispatches and their ledger steps are skipped and the sweep route runs next.
+
+## The sweep route
+
+The sweep runs once after every terminal decision, a review-1 PASS included, on the copy `sweep --prepare` prints, in a context that never opens the ledger folder.
+
+- Default: an Agent-tool subagent of the terminal ledger step (`ledger-steps/L-sweep-subagent.txt`), only after a recorded smoke check shows that a dispatched worker can spawn the subagent and keep sending its 5-minute heartbeat through a subagent run longer than 5 minutes.
+- Otherwise: `ledger-steps/L-sweep-prepare.txt`, then `T09b-sweep-dispatch.txt` as the sixth dispatch (declared as a deviation), then `ledger-steps/L-sweep-ingest.txt`.
+
+## Measurement rule
+
+`status` reports `metrics.headline_raw = U3 + W + O`: deferred, demoted and outside CRITICAL or MAJOR rows count as open (owner rule). `metrics.deferred_floor` is published beside it.
+
